        "notes": [
          "A session is listed when it came near the limit of its context window without a compaction, or was compacted at least 2 times.",
          "The saving is, on every main-agent request of these sessions, the input above the size of the session's first request: 109.0% of the period's cost (~$0.30 of ~$0.27). It assumes that the work could have started fresh at that size, so it is inferred.",
          "Fresh starts in the period: 2 after a recorded /clear (Claude Code), ~0 by the proxy for the clients that record none (a session that began at most 60 seconds after another of the same client, project and branch ended).",
          "The requests of these sessions are left out of the Context size saving, so the two savings add up.",
          "12 of the requests with a saving had no price for their model; they are priced at the period's average price per token class."
